 "text": "Hi, how are you holding up? That's usual for back pedal cranks. Some people live with it, others replace the part. A little on the chain and gears will leave a residue, so shower spray is the test. Spray first, then watch where it goes. Little goes a long way. Clean first with a mild soap, then let it dry completely. If it' your first clean, go ahead. Just don't start with solvent before the soap, it might interfere.",
